&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Python Senior Software Engineer to join the ATP team in Application Platform Domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, your mission will be to work on designing and delivering essential components that empower Doctolib teams to build robust and scalable services. You will be working in a feature team developing the chassis, archetypes, business-agnostic services, cross-cutting concerns and Claude Plugins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be working in a platform feature team developing the Python and Java/Kotlin chassis, project archetypes, business-agnostic services, cross-cutting concerns (resilience, security, observability…) and Claude Plugins, used by more than 60 services across Doctolib.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib involves building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients. We work in feature teams in an agile environment, while collaborating with product, design, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other engineers to define and implement features to improve the Doctolib platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a leading role within the team and contribute to establishing a technical vision that ensures the performance, security, and usability of the platform, taking into account the future needs and the high scalability needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring your expertise and experiences to help us continuously improve the way we implement, test, and monitor high-quality features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the performance of key features implemented in Python, sometimes completely challenging the status quo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking leadership on delivering roadmap items (together with the team)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to establishing a technical vision and co-drive the creation of the roadmap for next quarters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our tech environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our solutions are built on a single fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to the country and healthcare specialty requirements. To address these challenges, we are modularizing our platform run in a distributed architecture through reusable components.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack is composed of Rails, TypeScript, Java, Python, Kotlin, Swift, and React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on, if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are &lt;strong&gt;proactive, curious, collaborative&lt;/strong&gt; and eager to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are &lt;strong&gt;primarily a backend engineer&lt;/strong&gt; with expert knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a solid understanding of web technologies and software development life cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a &lt;strong&gt;“user first” mindset&lt;/strong&gt; and want to build a product focused on bringing value to its users, through &lt;strong&gt;secure, well-tested and pragmatic code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are &lt;strong&gt;fluent in English&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now it would be fantastic if you&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;have experience with Kafka and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;have experience with ADK and ML libraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;have experience with Java or Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free comprehensive health insurance for you and your children&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parent Care Program: additional leave on top of the legal parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free mental health and coaching services through our partner Moka.care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For caregivers and workers with disabilities, a package including an adaptation of the remote policy, extra days off for medical reasons, and psychological support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 14 days of RTT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A subsidy from the work council to refund part of the membership to a sport club or a creative class&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch voucher with Swile card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiter Interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feature Building Interview&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Design Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one reference check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permanent position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full Time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Levallois&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work setup (up to 2 remote days per week)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start date: As soon as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you would like to find out more about tech life at Doctolib, feel free to read our latest&lt;a href=&quot;https://medium.com/doctolib&quot;&gt; Medium blog articles&lt;/a&gt;!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Doctolib, we are committed to improving access to healthcare for everyone. This translates into our recruitment process. We evaluate candidates based solely on qualifications and motivation, without any form of discrimination.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The more diverse ideas are heard, the more our product will truly improve healthcare for all. You are welcome to apply to Doctolib, regardless of your gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To ensure equal opportunities, we invite you to exclude personal information (e.g. pictures, age) from your applications. If you require any accommodation, please let us know for support during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Join us in building the healthcare we all dream of!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All information provided is processed by Doctolib for application management. For data processing details, click here: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-DE&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Germany&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; l &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-FR&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;France&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; l &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-IT&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Italy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; l &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://doctolib.legal/B2C-Privacy-Policy-Career-COM&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Netherlands&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please contact hr.dataprivacy(at)doctolib.com for inquiries or to exercise your rights.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2013, Doctolib is Europe&#39;s leading AI and digital health company, serving 520,000 health professionals and 90 million people. We are building a new way to build software: agents doing the grunt work of writing, testing, reviewing and merging code, with engineers moving into a control-tower role to monitor and intervene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission: build the tooling and workflows that let AI agents and the engineers who work alongside them&amp;nbsp; test, review, ship and monitor code reliably, so Doctolib can multiply its engineering output while keeping quality and control.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director of Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our new &lt;strong&gt;AI Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt; team, reporting to the VP Platform Engineering. You will also own the existing CI and Developer Experience scope.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib is moving AI adoption from a temporary SWAT team to a permanent capability. The current team includes two Product Managers and two engineers, with more people joining through internal transfers and hiring.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your team will own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The agent-native testing and feedback infrastructure that lets agents know, within their own workflow, whether what they built is correct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD and build systems for the monolith and satellite services, elevated from a CI-run team into an efficient agent-testing capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer productivity measurement in the AI era DORA, autonomous change rate and complementary indicators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The inner-loop experience: local and remote environments, onboarding, editor integration and sandboxing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the tools and workflows that allow agents to write, test, review and merge code, including evaluation, security checks and controls — giving agents a fast, reliable feedback loop on whether what they build is correct.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own testing and feedback for the monolith and satellite services, elevating the current CI setup from a CI-run team into an efficient agent-testing capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own developer productivity measurement in the context of AI — DORA, autonomous change rate and complementary indicators — and make it visible and actionable to feature teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the inner-loop experience: local and remote environments, onboarding, editor integration and sandboxing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and organise the team, developing agentic skills internally where needed, as AI adoption shifts from a temporary SWAT team to a permanent one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering and Product Management to understand internal users and drive adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the VP Platform Engineering, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/maidane/&quot;&gt;Mike Aidane&lt;/a&gt;, you&#39;ll join the Platform Engineering leadership team alongside directors and senior EMs for Application Platform, Data Services and Platform Services.&lt;strong&gt; You will lead the new AI Developer Experience team&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll partner closely with Product Engineering, Product Management, Release Engineering, Quality Engineering, Automation Platform, Infrastructure Platform, SRE, FinOps, Security, Privacy and Compliance, and engineering teams across France and Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have&lt;strong&gt; led engineering organisations through large-scale Developer Experience transformations&lt;/strong&gt; and know what it takes to ship great tooling fast, durably, and without sacrificing quality. You think in systems&amp;nbsp;technical and organisational and are as comfortable setting architecture direction as you are making a hard technical call.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have&lt;strong&gt; led Developer Experience, Developer Productivity, Developer Infrastructure or Build/CI organisations serving 300+ engineers. &lt;/strong&gt;You have demonstrated measurable change in how engineers work, with evidence of adoption, productivity outcomes and organisational or operating-model change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep technical credibility across CI/CD, build and test infrastructure, monorepo build graphs, test selection, caching, merge queues and flake management. You can guide architecture and trade-offs while remaining credible with Staff Engineers and strong EMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;5+ years of experience as a manager of managers:&lt;/strong&gt; hiring, growing and levelling engineering managers and staff-plus ICs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable setting your own success metrics and being held to them, with strong written communication and structured thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent exposure to AI-assisted or agentic engineering transformation, including evaluation, security, guardrails, adoption and productivity measurement. Several years of AI Developer Experience leadership are not expected — the relevant signal is strong large-scale DevEx experience combined with recent AI transformation exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large legacy codebases or monoliths, or in a regulated or high-trust environment such as healthcare. You treat constraints as design inputs, not blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
